# The pipeline fixture's bytes are pinned: tests pin the committed files
# byte-for-byte against their generator, and the gate copies them into the
# measured mini-tree, so no eol translation may touch them on checkout --
# without this, a Windows autocrlf checkout turns the LF fixture into CRLF
# on disk and the byte pin fails. Other text files keep the default
# handling unless specified below (blobs are LF in-repo either way).
tests/fixtures/pipeline/* -text
# Keep the tracker's byte-stable seed in its writer's LF format on checkout.
data/openrouter-trending.json text eol=lf
